{
  "_note": "USD per 1M tokens. Prices change — verify on https://www.anthropic.com/pricing and https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing and edit this file. 'match' is a case-insensitive regex tested against the normalized model name; first match wins, so keep specific patterns (e.g. flash-lite) above generic ones. 'context_window' is the conversation's token limit in Antigravity as known at release — the maxContextTokens its generator metadata and agent-state stream report (verified on Antigravity 2.35.1, 2026-11-25); Antigravity sets it on its servers, so usage.py shows the window it gave the latest call and the newest one recorded per model (hooks/context_window.py, ~/.gemini/antigravity-plus/context-windows.json), then the window the client's own model list gives (hooks/client.py), before this number: 512k for Gemini 4 (Neon, Carbon, Argon, Hydrogen, Orchestrators and executors), 256k for Gemini 3.8/3.6/3 Flash & 3.1 Pro, 128k for 3.5/3.1 Flash-Lite and Gemini 2.5 (the client's list on 2.35.2, 2026-11-27), 840k for Claude 5.5 (1M API window), 80k for GPT-OSS 120B; the native API window is 'api_context_window'. Antigravity compacts when the next model call won't fit the window (or, in the Antigravity CLI only, its AGY_CLI_AUTO_COMPACT_OVERRIDE setting). 'compaction_threshold' (optional) is only for models compacting well below their window. 'price_changes' entries ({from: 'YYYY-MM-DD', …prices}) apply to calls made on or after that local date. 'service_tiers' (Gemini API batch / flex / priority / contributor) are used only with usage.py --tier. Orchestrator (fixed or configurable Planner/Executor in Settings > Models) prices planner calls at the planner's model and executor calls at the executor's model (Gemini 4 Hydrogen or Claude Sonnet 5.5).",
  "_updated": "2026-11-27",
